# What does NOT go to pub.dev.
#
# A .pubignore REPLACES .gitignore for publishing: when this file exists, pub
# stops honouring .gitignore entirely. So everything that must stay out of the
# archive has to be named here, including things git already ignores. Anything
# hidden only by .git/info/exclude is invisible to pub twice over, because that
# file is machine-local and is not in the repository at all.

.idea
*.iml
.dart_tool/
.claude/
pubspec_overrides.yaml

# Rust build artifacts. 116 MB on disk, 41 MB compressed, and useless to a
# consumer: they are objects for the machine that built them. The crate's
# source stays, so anyone can build the accelerator themselves.
native/stark_kernels/target/

# Development-only: planning artifacts, design notes, one-off probes.
docs/
openspec/
tool/

# Kernel libraries built for a release, which ship from GitHub, not pub.dev.
dist/
